```swift
func greeting(_ name: String?) -> String {
    if let present = name {
        return "Hello, \(present)"
    }
    return "Guest"
}
print(greeting("Mira"))
print(greeting(nil))
```
The outputs are `Hello, Mira` and `Guest`. The first call has a name. The second has no name, so it uses the fallback.
